+On Linux, a writable host volume whose files carry
+`user.containers.override_stat` metadata can opt in per mount with
+`-v /host/website:/website-workspaces:override-stat`, or with
+`"overrideStat": true` on that mount in the HTTP create request. The choice
+is persisted across machine restarts; other mounts keep their normal ownership
+and mode handling. The selected volume requires a libkrun that exports
+`krun_add_virtiofs4` and a host filesystem that supports the xattr.
+
 **Use git and SSH without copying private keys into the guest.** Forward your host SSH agent into the VM. The guest can ask the agent to sign with any forwarded key while the socket is available, so forward it only to workloads you trust. Requires an SSH agent running on your host (`ssh-add -l` to check).
 
